  "summary": "Backstage: Improper input validation in cloud storage URL readers",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker with write access to a cloud storage bucket used by Backstage could craft object names that could collide with protected files in the output directory. In certain deployment configurations, this could lead to content injection.\n\n### Patches\n\nPatched in `@backstage/backend-defaults` version `0.17.8`",
